commit 95d8b36f3959543eb78ec1dcb4e3583042ec2f85
Author: Abhinav S V <abhinavsv3@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 23:11:48 2026 -0700

    Rust: detect Cargo.toml, name integration-test targets, parse cargo test output
    
    Python, Go and JavaScript were supported; Rust repos have unusually good
    test discipline and the detection is one file.
    
    Stable cargo has no JSON test output, so the runner's text is parsed:
    `test name ... ok|FAILED|ignored`, with names qualified by the target
    being run so two integration files defining test_basic do not collide.
    tests/<name>.rs maps to --test <name>; anything deeper is a module of a
    target the path alone cannot name, so every test runs rather than
    silently none. A crate that fails to compile prints no test lines, which
    puts the whole target in FAIL_TO_PASS -- the same shape as Go, and the
    same reason Rust defaults to full PASS_TO_PASS scope.
    
    Unit tests inside src/ share a file with the code under test and cannot
    be mined; the plan says so. Tested at the unit level only: this machine
    has no cargo, so #31 stays open until someone validates a real crate.
    
    Refs #31
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

